## Docker

{% if choices.docker == "full" -%}
Mode: **everything in Docker**. `docker-compose.yml` has two services:

- `dev` (profile `dev`, stage `dev` of `Dockerfile`): mounts the project at `/app`, keeps `node_modules` in the named volume `node_modules`, runs as user `node`, reads `.env` and publishes `WEB_PORT`; Vite binds to `0.0.0.0` and polls for file changes. `docker compose up dev` runs `npm run dev`; `docker compose run --rm dev npm …` runs any script. After changing dependencies run `docker compose run --rm dev npm ci` (or `npm install <pkg>`).
- `app`: the production image (see below), `docker compose up --build app`.
{%- else -%}
Mode: **Docker to run the app**. Development happens on the host with Node.js (`npm run dev`); Docker builds and serves the production game.
{%- endif %}

- `Dockerfile` (multi-stage, `node:24-bookworm-slim`): `dev` installs dependencies, `build` runs `vite build` with `APP_NAME`/`APP_SLUG` build arguments, `production` contains only `dist/`, `scripts/` and `package.json` and runs `node scripts/serve.mjs` as user `node` on port 5173 inside the container. `.env` is never copied into the image.
- `docker-compose.yml` reads `.env`: `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` ({{ project.slug }}) names the stack, `APP_NAME`/`APP_SLUG` are build arguments, and `WEB_PORT` is the published host port. The title is baked in at build time: rebuild (`docker compose up --build app`) after changing it.
- Saves live in the player's browser, so there is no data volume.
- Commands: `docker compose up --build app`, `docker compose build app`, `docker compose{% if choices.docker == "full" %} --profile dev{% endif %} logs -f`, `docker compose{% if choices.docker == "full" %} --profile dev{% endif %} down`. `docker compose --profile dev down --volumes --remove-orphans --rmi local` removes the containers, the dependency volume and the local images.
{% endif %}
